module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_valid_let_is_refused_as_let_body_not_reachable_from_node_with_a_spanless_locus

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data a_valid_let_is_refused_as_let_body_not_reachable_from_node_with_a_spanless_locus: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_valid_let_is_refused_as_let_body_not_reachable_from_node_with_a_spanless_locus" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundBelowTheLadder, ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "v2 body lowering reaches a let's body from the let's own grammar position on every route a valid module uses, so no accepted v1 module is refused with body_lowering_reason_let_body_not_reachable_from_node; and every refusal any v2 stage emits at a NodeLocus carries the textual extent of the node it refuses, so a refusal names the declaration it refuses (the let case and the v2.compiler.infer groundings are two producers of this one class)" } },

  receipts: [
    "**v2 normalize REFUSES an unchanged, valid module with body_lowering_reason_let_body_not_reachable_from_node, and the refusal's locus is a NodeLocus with no textual extent.** INVALID STATE: a module the seed accepts and executes is refused by v2's own front end. That refusal names no declaration and no position. HARM: every consumer that runs the v2 front end over the module refuses it as a whole, and none can say where: the generated roster import sweep (v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep, RefusalNormalizeRefused: 'REFUSE <path> normalize-refused'), the namespace-wave binding census, and native resolve. A wave then has to hand-apply what its generator should have placed, and the cause stays unlocated. Emitted by v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold body_lower_let_expr when body_lower_unwrap_captured finds the let's shell.",
    "RECEIPT 2026-10-25 (warm-pike-481, PR #15126, the sha256_hex_of_text home wave). MODULE: test.claim.host_custody_export_receipt_witness (dag/test/claim/host_custody_export_receipt_witness.dag), unchanged at source commit 0d417c2534599c28374754d63e807ac4a0e3b7e7. ROUTE: a probe running exactly the sweep's front end -- tokenize_prepared, parse_module_prepared, normalize_with(source: NormalizeWithIsolatedAllocator, spans: the parse artifact's span index) -- under `gunbc run --function normalize_refusal_probe_exit --arg path=<module>`. It prints one diagnostic: reason body_lowering_reason_let_body_not_reachable_from_node, at a NodeLocus. SEED: gunbc built from that commit in a private target dir on srv1, sha256 2a23190f68eb04303201b641bdd8c546d75372bb209fa928588446082c417252, re-hashed OK after the run. The same probe on dag/gunbc/oracle_oci/api.dag and dag/gunbc/machine_intake/mtjade1_access_observation.dag prints body_lowering_reason_uses_clause_unmodeled, which is the D13 frontier (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode uses_clause_has_no_carrier) and not this class. The wave hand-applied `import std.content_hash { sha256_hex_of_text }` to all three, as ruled by tidy-ant-251.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder, as ruled by tidy-ant-251: a valid program refused at the front end, with the refusal's location missing. CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- the let body's position is a grammar fact, read positionally or refused at a located extent. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: as stated in the standing; it is climbable now but unbuilt, and goes to the first free binding/front-end slot (tidy-ant-251). The discriminating RED is the unchanged module above, refused today. The positive control that pairs with it is OWED, not run here: the same probe accepting a module whose let the seed and v2 both read the same way.",

    "SECOND PRODUCER OF THE SAME CLASS, v2.compiler.infer (2026-11-04, jolly-cat-271, srv2 jc299-mbt1r-3882, claim_batch sha256 490947437bf9070b3b20a70e6abe9e6196e9bb20c390524ec5dbcdfddba279db, ARITY-PATCHED PROBE, NOT THE TREE, at 388263b185c397a4b75ddc23a272ca53dcc71a3d): infer rejecting the 49-line v2.test.claim.match_binder.match_binder_typing fixture program reports 45 diagnostics, 44 infer_grounding_not_derived and 1 inhabitance_structural_roots_differ, and EVERY one is a NodeLocus with no textual extent, so the refusal cannot name which of the fixture's declarations it refuses. The one rejecting reason is therefore unlocated (DESIGN 5 requires typed, LOCATED): the declaration was recovered only by reading the source (candidate g_constructor, declared ParseTree, arms construct Outcome), not from the diagnostic. This widens the class beyond the let body: the missing locus is a property of NodeLocus refusals from any stage, so the trigger in the rung standing above names the capability for all producers.",
    "GENERAL CLASS (jolly-cat-271, 2026-11-04, DESIGN 6b root generalization, per tidy-ant-251 msg_1aa030bb): a NodeLocus refusal with no extent. The two receipts above are two producers (v2 normalize body lowering for a let; v2.compiler.infer for 45 groundings and a declared-return refusal) of one rule: a refusal at a NodeLocus names an anchor but no byte range, so the located-diagnostic obligation of DESIGN 5 is unmet wherever the anchor has no span. The sibling producers beyond these two are not enumerated here; the discriminator for a new producer is any Rejected diagnostic whose at is NodeLocus and whose source module is unchanged. The infer producer cost the match_binder_typing arms a diagnosis that read the fixture source by hand (jc299, then jc300 showed the declared return was the defect, jc301 the tree green at dd550e8df76e391c899ad79e161f678f44638995 with 20 of 20 claims PASS)."
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold", decl_name: "body_lower_let_expr", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.host_custody_export_receipt_witness", decl_name: "live_tree_disposition", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
